\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-4:4,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4.2,0)--(4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black] (-3,0)--(-3,-0.12) (0,0)--(0,-0.12);
\path (-3,-0.12) node[below] {$240$} (0,-0.12) node[below] {$\mu$} (-3.1,0.9) node {$0.0013$} (1.5,-0.65) node {Volume (mL)};
\draw[black,->] (-3.1,0.65)--(-3.45,0.04);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}-3&=\frac{240-\mu}{3}\\-9&=240-\mu\\\mu&=249\end{aligned}$
Set the mean to $249$ mL. The cutoff is three standard deviations below this mean.

Convert to a left-hand probability.
$\begin{aligned}P(X<72)&=1-0.9332\\&=0.0668\end{aligned}$
Since this is below $0.5$, the cutoff lies below the mean. Symmetry and the table give $z=-1.5$.
